IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `tad-dates`
IMPORT `tad-rules`
IMPORT `tad-seat`

-- Anti-Discrimination Act 1998 (Tas) -- worked cases for the questions of the person aggrieved (tad-seat.l4). Every
-- expected value was worked by hand from the deposited text; none was copied from the encoding's output. Each assertion
-- is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. The facts are illustrative.
-- UNOFFICIAL. Based on material from the Tasmanian Legislation website (State of Tasmania, CC BY 4.0). BASELINE
-- ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `cases`

`d` MEANS `the calendar date`
`nd` MEANS `d` 1 1 2000

§§ `Prescribed attributes (s 16)`

#ASSERT `Is it a prescribed attribute` `disability` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is it a prescribed attribute` `irrelevant medical record` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is it a prescribed attribute` `association with a person who has, or is believed to have, any of these attributes` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is it a prescribed attribute` `something else not listed` EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `Direct and indirect discrimination (ss 14, 15, 22)`

-- A worker refused a promotion because of her pregnancy.
#ASSERT `Was I directly discriminated against` `pregnancy` `employment` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Treated no less favourably: "takes place if" fails.
#ASSERT `Was I directly discriminated against` `pregnancy` `employment` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A reason the Act does not list.
#ASSERT `Was I directly discriminated against` `something else not listed` `employment` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Outside every area of s 22(1): not answered.
#ASSERT `Was I directly discriminated against` `race` `none of these areas` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A height requirement for a job that is unreasonable and disadvantages women more.
#ASSERT `Was I indirectly discriminated against` `gender` `employment` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The same requirement, reasonable in the circumstances.
#ASSERT `Was I indirectly discriminated against` `gender` `employment` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- No group disadvantage.
#ASSERT `Was I indirectly discriminated against` `gender` `employment` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Was I indirectly discriminated against` `something else not listed` `accommodation` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Was I indirectly discriminated against` `disability` `none of these areas` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Offensive conduct (s 17(1))`

-- Ridicule of a customer's disability in a shop.
#ASSERT `Was the offensive conduct prohibited` `disability` `provision of facilities, goods and services` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Religious belief is not among the attributes s 17(1) names.
#ASSERT `Was the offensive conduct prohibited` `religious belief or affiliation` `provision of facilities, goods and services` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Industrial activity is not among them either.
#ASSERT `Was the offensive conduct prohibited` `industrial activity` `employment` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A reasonable person would not have anticipated offence: outside the prohibition's words.
#ASSERT `Was the offensive conduct prohibited` `age` `employment` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Was the offensive conduct prohibited` `age` `none of these areas` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Sexual harassment (s 17(2), (3))`

#ASSERT `Was I sexually harassed` `a remark or statement with sexual connotations, to me or about me in my presence (s 17(3)(c))` `employment` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Was I sexually harassed` `physical contact of a sexual nature (s 17(3)(a))` `education and training` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Welcome conduct is not harassment.
#ASSERT `Was I sexually harassed` `a sexual advance or a request for sexual favours (s 17(3)(b))` `employment` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- No reasonable anticipation of offence.
#ASSERT `Was I sexually harassed` `a gesture, action or comment of a sexual nature (s 17(3)(d))` `employment` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Was I sexually harassed` `none of these` `employment` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Was I sexually harassed` `other conduct of a sexual nature in relation to me (s 17(3)(e))` `none of these areas` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Victimisation (s 18)`

#ASSERT `Was I victimised` TRUE `I made, or intend to make, a complaint under the Act` `employment` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Was I victimised` TRUE `I refused, or intend to refuse, to do something that would contravene the Act` `employment` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Was I victimised` FALSE `I made, or intend to make, a complaint under the Act` `employment` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Was I victimised` TRUE `another reason` `employment` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Was I victimised` TRUE `I gave, or intend to give, evidence or information in proceedings under the Act` `none of these areas` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Inciting hatred (s 19)`

#ASSERT `Was it inciting hatred` `race` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Was it inciting hatred` `sex characteristics` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Age is not a s 19 ground.
#ASSERT `Was it inciting hatred` `age` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Not a public act.
#ASSERT `Was it inciting hatred` `race` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Advertisements (s 20)`

#ASSERT `Was the advertisement prohibited` TRUE TRUE FALSE `employment` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- An anti-discrimination poster that depicts discrimination to discourage it.
#ASSERT `Was the advertisement prohibited` TRUE TRUE TRUE `employment` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Was the advertisement prohibited` TRUE FALSE FALSE `accommodation` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Who is liable (ss 21, 104)`

#ASSERT `Is the helper liable too` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the helper liable too` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Is the helper liable too` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Is the organisation liable` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the organisation liable` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Is the organisation liable` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Exceptions (Part 5, s 101)`

-- s 41: race, a genuine occupational qualification.
#ASSERT `Does the exception cover it` `s 41: race, employment, a genuine occupational qualification` `race` TRUE TRUE FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does the exception cover it` `s 41: race, employment, a genuine occupational qualification` `race` TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does the exception cover it` `s 41: race, employment, a genuine occupational qualification` `age` TRUE TRUE FALSE 0 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Does the exception cover it` `s 41: race, employment, a genuine occupational qualification` `race` FALSE TRUE FALSE 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 27(1)(e): shared accommodation for 4 adults, and for 5.
#ASSERT `Does the exception cover it` `s 27(1)(e): gender, in shared accommodation for fewer than 5 adults` `gender` TRUE TRUE FALSE 4 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does the exception cover it` `s 27(1)(e): gender, in shared accommodation for fewer than 5 adults` `gender` TRUE TRUE FALSE 5 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 29: one-gender competition, a player of 12 and of 11 (s 29 names no ground).
#ASSERT `Does the exception cover it` `s 29: competitive sport restricted to one gender aged 12 or more` `gender` TRUE FALSE FALSE 12 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does the exception cover it` `s 29: competitive sport restricted to one gender aged 12 or more` `gender` TRUE FALSE FALSE 11 EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 39: a child of 17, and a person of 18.
#ASSERT `Does the exception cover it` `s 39: age, a child required to be accompanied by an adult` `age` TRUE TRUE FALSE 17 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does the exception cover it` `s 39: age, a child required to be accompanied by an adult` `age` TRUE FALSE FALSE 17 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does the exception cover it` `s 39: age, a child required to be accompanied by an adult` `age` TRUE TRUE FALSE 18 EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 30(1)(b): actuarial data, with and without disclosure to the Tribunal (s 30(2)).
#ASSERT `Does the exception cover it` `s 30(1)(b): gender, marital or relationship status, insurance or superannuation, actuarial or statistical data` `gender` TRUE TRUE TRUE 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does the exception cover it` `s 30(1)(b): gender, marital or relationship status, insurance or superannuation, actuarial or statistical data` `gender` TRUE TRUE FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does the exception cover it` `s 30(1)(b): gender, marital or relationship status, insurance or superannuation, actuarial or statistical data` `disability` TRUE TRUE TRUE 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 44: disability and insurance.
#ASSERT `Does the exception cover it` `s 44: disability, annuity, insurance or superannuation, actuarial or statistical data` `disability` TRUE TRUE TRUE 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does the exception cover it` `s 44: disability, annuity, insurance or superannuation, actuarial or statistical data` `disability` TRUE FALSE TRUE 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 33(1)(a): prescribed standards need no disclosure.
#ASSERT `Does the exception cover it` `s 33(1)(a): age, superannuation, Commonwealth prescribed standards` `age` TRUE TRUE FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 51A(1): admission to a religious school; an enrolled student; another ground (s 51A(3)).
#ASSERT `Does the exception cover it` `s 51A(1): religion, admission as a student to a religious educational institution` `religious belief or affiliation` TRUE FALSE TRUE 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does the exception cover it` `s 51A(1): religion, admission as a student to a religious educational institution` `religious belief or affiliation` TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does the exception cover it` `s 51A(1): religion, admission as a student to a religious educational institution` `race` TRUE FALSE TRUE 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does the exception cover it` `s 51A(1): religion, admission as a student to a religious educational institution` `religious activity` FALSE FALSE TRUE 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 35: retirement.
#ASSERT `Does the exception cover it` `s 35: age, retirement or voluntary severance` `age` TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does the exception cover it` `s 35: age, retirement or voluntary severance` `age` FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 24: any ground.
#ASSERT `Does the exception cover it` `s 24: reasonably necessary to comply with a law or an order` `race` TRUE TRUE FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does the exception cover it` `s 24: reasonably necessary to comply with a law or an order` `race` TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 28: pregnancy and unjustifiable hardship; disability is not its ground.
#ASSERT `Does the exception cover it` `s 28: family, parental, pregnancy, breastfeeding, marital or relationship status, special services imposing unjustifiable hardship` `pregnancy` TRUE TRUE FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does the exception cover it` `s 28: family, parental, pregnancy, breastfeeding, marital or relationship status, special services imposing unjustifiable hardship` `disability` TRUE TRUE FALSE 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 27(2): a club benefit, not provided separately or in fair proportion.
#ASSERT `Does the exception cover it` `s 27(2): gender, the use of a club benefit` `gender` TRUE TRUE FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does the exception cover it` `s 27(2): gender, the use of a club benefit` `gender` TRUE TRUE TRUE 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 52(d): an act in accordance with doctrine and necessary to avoid offence is the setting; outside it, NOTHING (F5).
#ASSERT `Does the exception cover it` `s 52(d): religion, another act in accordance with religious doctrine` `religious belief or affiliation` TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does the exception cover it` `s 52(d): religion, another act in accordance with religious doctrine` `religious belief or affiliation` FALSE TRUE TRUE 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 53, s 45(a), s 54 and a granted exemption.
#ASSERT `Does the exception cover it` `s 53: political belief or activity, employment as an adviser or political staff` `political activity` TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does the exception cover it` `s 45(a): disability, employment, inherent requirements or unjustifiable hardship` `disability` TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does the exception cover it` `s 54: age or disability, legal incapacity` `age` TRUE TRUE FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does the exception cover it` `an exemption granted by the Commissioner (ss 56, 57)` `gender` TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does the exception cover it` `an exemption granted by the Commissioner (ss 56, 57)` `gender` FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Public purpose (s 55)`

#ASSERT `Does the public purpose exception cover it` `inciting hatred (s 19)` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does the public purpose exception cover it` `conduct that offended, humiliated, intimidated, insulted or ridiculed me (s 17(1))` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does the public purpose exception cover it` `inciting hatred (s 19)` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does the public purpose exception cover it` `other conduct` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

