#ASSERT `By when can I seek review of an exemption` (`d` 1 3 2026) EQUALS `d` 29 3 2026

§§ `Who may complain (ss 60, 60A)`

#ASSERT `May the complaint be made` `the person it was directed against (s 60(1)(a))` 30 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A child of 17 without, and with, the Commissioner's satisfaction; a person of 18.
#ASSERT `May the complaint be made` `the person it was directed against (s 60(1)(a))` 17 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `May the complaint be made` `the person it was directed against (s 60(1)(a))` 17 FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May the complaint be made` `the person it was directed against (s 60(1)(a))` 18 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A litigation guardian for a child of 10.
#ASSERT `May the complaint be made` `a litigation guardian appointed by the Commissioner (s 60A)` 10 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A class complaint, with and without the Commissioner's satisfaction about consent.
#ASSERT `May the complaint be made` `the person it was directed against, for a class of people it was also directed against (s 60(1)(b))` 40 TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May the complaint be made` `the person it was directed against, for a class of people it was also directed against (s 60(1)(b))` 40 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `May the complaint be made` `an organisation it was directed against (s 60(1)(d))` 99 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- On another's behalf, with and without approval (s 60(4)): a union for one member, an agent, anyone else (F15).
#ASSERT `May the complaint be made` `a trade union, for one member it was directed against (s 60(1)(c)(i))` 99 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `May the complaint be made` `a trade union, for one member it was directed against (s 60(1)(c)(i))` 99 FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May the complaint be made` `an agent of one of these (s 60(1)(e))` 40 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `May the complaint be made` `an agent of one of these (s 60(1)(e))` 40 FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May the complaint be made` `another person on behalf of the person it was directed against (s 60(1)(f))` 50 FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May the complaint be made` `another person on behalf of the person it was directed against (s 60(1)(f))` 50 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `May the complaint be made` `someone else` 50 TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Bars to complaining (ss 66, 68, 73, 108)`

#ASSERT `Can I still complain` FALSE `nothing earlier` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I still complain` TRUE `nothing earlier` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I still complain` FALSE `I agreed with them not to complain (s 66)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I still complain` FALSE `I agreed with them not to complain (s 66)` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I still complain` FALSE `I withdrew a complaint about the same matter (s 68(6))` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I still complain` FALSE `I withdrew a complaint about the same matter, but not voluntarily (s 68(7))` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I still complain` FALSE `an earlier complaint about the same matter lapsed (ss 65(4), 71(5), 72(1))` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `Form (s 62)`

#ASSERT `Is my complaint in the required form` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my complaint in the required form` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my complaint in the required form` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `Time limit (s 63)`

#ASSERT `By when must I complain` (`d` 15 3 2025) EQUALS `d` 15 3 2026
-- 29 February: the next year has none, so 28 February (fork F1).
#ASSERT `By when must I complain` (`d` 29 2 2024) EQUALS `d` 28 2 2025
#ASSERT `By when must I complain` (`d` 31 1 2025) EQUALS `d` 31 1 2026
-- The last day, the day after, the day of the conduct, and the day before it.
#ASSERT `Is my complaint in time` (`d` 15 3 2025) (`d` 15 3 2026) EQUALS `in time`
#ASSERT `Is my complaint in time` (`d` 15 3 2025) (`d` 16 3 2026) EQUALS `late, but the Commissioner may accept it if satisfied that it is reasonable to do so (s 63(2))`
#ASSERT `Is my complaint in time` (`d` 15 3 2025) (`d` 15 3 2025) EQUALS `in time`
#ASSERT `Is my complaint in time` (`d` 15 3 2025) (`d` 14 3 2025) EQUALS `not answered: that day is before the conduct`
-- From 29 February 2024: 28 February 2025 in time, 1 March 2025 late.
#ASSERT `Is my complaint in time` (`d` 29 2 2024) (`d` 28 2 2025) EQUALS `in time`
#ASSERT `Is my complaint in time` (`d` 29 2 2024) (`d` 1 3 2025) EQUALS `late, but the Commissioner may accept it if satisfied that it is reasonable to do so (s 63(2))`

§§ `Acceptance or rejection (s 64)`

#ASSERT `Can my complaint be rejected` `trivial, vexatious, misconceived or lacking in substance, in the Commissioner's opinion (s 64(1)(a))` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can my complaint be rejected` `trivial, vexatious, misconceived or lacking in substance, in the Commissioner's opinion (s 64(1)(a))` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can my complaint be rejected` `I have started proceedings elsewhere on the same events, with similar remedies (s 64(1)(c))` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can my complaint be rejected` `none of these` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Received 1 July 2026: 42 days after is 12 August 2026.
#ASSERT `By when must my complaint be accepted or rejected` (`d` 1 7 2026) EQUALS `d` 12 8 2026

§§ `Review by the Tribunal (ss 65, 71, 72, 73)`

-- Statement received 10 January 2026: 28 days after is 7 February 2026.
#ASSERT `By when must I apply for review` (`d` 10 1 2026) EQUALS `d` 7 2 2026
#ASSERT `Is my review application in time` (`d` 10 1 2026) (`d` 7 2 2026) EQUALS `in time`
#ASSERT `Is my review application in time` (`d` 10 1 2026) (`d` 8 2 2026) EQUALS `too late: the complaint has lapsed, and you cannot complain again about the same matter (ss 65(4), 71(5), 73)`
#ASSERT `Is my review application in time` (`d` 10 1 2026) (`d` 9 1 2026) EQUALS `not answered: that day is before the statement was received`
#ASSERT `What happens after review` `my complaint was rejected (s 64)` TRUE EQUALS `the complaint lapses, and you cannot complain again about the same matter (ss 72(1), 73)`
#ASSERT `What happens after review` `my complaint was rejected (s 64)` FALSE EQUALS `the complaint goes back to the Commissioner for investigation (s 72(2))`
#ASSERT `What happens after review` `my complaint was dismissed after investigation (s 71)` FALSE EQUALS `the Tribunal deals with the complaint as an inquiry (s 72(3))`
#ASSERT `What happens after review` `my complaint was not accepted` FALSE EQUALS `the complaint goes back to the Commissioner to accept or reject it (s 72(4))`

§§ `Referral and appeal (ss 78, 100)`

-- Notified 31 August 2025: 6 months on, February has no 31st, so 28 February 2026 (fork F1).
#ASSERT `By when must my complaint be referred` (`d` 31 8 2025) FALSE `nd` EQUALS `d` 28 2 2026
#ASSERT `By when must my complaint be referred` (`d` 15 7 2026) FALSE `nd` EQUALS `d` 15 1 2027
#ASSERT `By when must my complaint be referred` (`d` 15 7 2026) TRUE (`d` 1 6 2027) EQUALS `d` 1 6 2027
-- Decision 20 December 2026: 28 days after is 17 January 2027.
#ASSERT `By when can I appeal a dismissal for not pursuing` (`d` 20 12 2026) EQUALS `d` 17 1 2027
#ASSERT `Is my appeal in time` (`d` 20 12 2026) (`d` 17 1 2027) EQUALS `in time`
#ASSERT `Is my appeal in time` (`d` 20 12 2026) (`d` 18 1 2027) EQUALS `too late: the 28 days in s 100(2) have passed`
#ASSERT `Is my appeal in time` (`d` 20 12 2026) (`d` 19 12 2026) EQUALS `not answered: that day is before the decision`

